    "description": "**Faculty.Professor.Research Associate \\- Full\\-Time**\n\n\nMed\\-Psychiatry \\- Pennsylvania\\-Pittsburgh \\- (26004224\\) **Research Associate Professor of Psychiatry**\n\n**University of Pittsburgh, Department of Psychiatry**  \n\nPittsburgh, United States\n\n**Job Description**\n\n\nThe Department of Psychiatry at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking a full\\-time **Research Associate Professor** in the appointment stream to contribute to and advance research in psychiatric illness and mental health.\n\n\nThe incumbent's responsibilities will include:\n\n* Conducting independent and collaborative research focused on the neurobiological substrates of complex human cognitive functions and how alterations in these systems contribute to cognitive dysfunction.\n* Developing and leading innovative research initiatives, including the design, execution, and dissemination of research studies.\n* Preparing manuscripts for publication in peer\\-reviewed journals and serving as a co\\-investigator on externally funded research projects.\n* Providing scientific leadership within a multidisciplinary research environment.\n* Overseeing aspects of laboratory operations, including project management, supervision of research staff, and mentorship of graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and junior investigators.\n* Ensuring all research activities are conducted in accordance with university, federal, and other applicable guidelines governing the responsible conduct of research.\n\n\nThe search committee will primarily be looking for demonstrated experience in:\n\n* Leading collaborative research initiatives and contributing substantially to a strong publication record.\n* Contributing to extramural research funding.\n* Scientific leadership and effective collaboration within interdisciplinary research teams.\n* Demonstrated excellence in mentoring and training students, trainees, and research staff.\n\n\nSuccessful candidates will join a vibrant and highly interactive research community with a long history of excellence in basic and translational neuroscience research.\n\n**Qualifications**\n\n* PhD in Neuroscience, Psychology, or a related field.\n* Demonstrated expertise in psychiatry research, as evidenced by a sustained record of peer\\-reviewed publications.\n* Evidence of scholarly achievement and research impact.\n* Evidence of success in contributing to competitive research funding.\n* Strong organizational, leadership, and project management skills.\n* Ability to work effectively in a dynamic and growing academic environment.\n\n**About the Employer**\n\n\nAt the University of Pittsburgh Department of Psychiatry, we excel in our mission to:\n\n* Provide superb behavioral health services to our patients and their families;\n* Pursue the development of improved diagnostic techniques and therapeutic interventions through innovative research;\n* Provide a stimulating learning environment for medical and graduate students, residents, psychology interns, and postdoctoral fellows.\n\n\nOur success in each of these areas depends on a highly interactive community of clinicians, scientists, and educators who bring diversity in background, experience, expertise, and perspective to our mission.\n\n\nAn essential partner in this work is UPMC Western Psychiatric Hospital, a national leader in innovative treatment of mental health and addiction disorders. Pitt Psychiatry's faculty of more than 230 members across basic and clinical science disciplines is central to our success in advancing research, education, and clinical care.\n\n**Areas of Research**\n\n* Psychology\n* Psychiatry\n* Neuroscience\n\n**How to Apply**\n\n\nPlease apply by going to our job site (https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt\\_faculty\\_external/jobsearch.ftl), searching job code 26004224 in the keyword search, and submitting your materials through our Pitt system.\n\n\nThe University of Pittsburgh is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and values equality of opportunity, human dignity, and diversity, EOE, including disability/vets.\n\n *The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran.*\n\n  \n\n**Assignment Category****:** Full\\-time regular**Campus****:** Pittsburgh**Child Protection Clearances****:** The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance.**Required Attachments****:** Curriculum Vitae",
